Harden the CIX Sky1 NPU descriptor envelope and global controls.

Validate the documented V3 head/first/last TCB types after pinning the
submitting file's allocation.  Keep destructive controls privileged and
account tick-counter requests per open file.  Reject the timeout-job ioctl
on V3, where the public ABI defines it as unsupported, and refuse a
file-local close abort while the shared command pool contains another
file's work.  Restore the R2P0 ABI's V3 debug-dispatch operation with
validated flags and core selection, an isolated idle command pool, and
complete pool-state rollback when hardware reservation fails.

The public descriptor schema does not define every nested payload pointer.
Mapped TCBs remain writable after submission.  This change therefore does
not claim complete validation of a hostile userspace descriptor graph.

Provenance: overlay-created from the audited Arm China R2P0 and R2P1
sources.

